<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Rendering Wireframe and Wireframe Mode</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p><span class="Command">Rendering Wireframe</span> <span lang="EN-GB">is accessible from the</span> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>tree context menu &gt; Rendering &gt; Wireframe</b></span></i><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p><span class="Mode" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Polygons</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">mode is accessible from the</span> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>viewport context menu &gt; Render Mode &gt; Polygons</b></span></i> <span lang="EN-GB">or by pressing</span> <b><span class="Shortcut" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>3</b></span></b><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><span lang="EN-GB" class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">These commands affect visual representation of scan data, meshes, and polylines. When in this mode, KUBE draws objects as connected triangles. Triangles are used for scan data and meshes only. Polylines are drawn as connected lines.</span></p>
<p><span class="Command">Rendering Wireframe</span> <span lang="EN-GB">is applied to a particular entity (or group of entities) from which the context menu was called.</span></p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Wireframe</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">mode is applied to all scan data, meshes, and polylines in the scene.</span></p>
